;; The capacity experiment (capacity.yml, bb capacity): every runner races from spawn to the
;; nether while bots join in steps, ten and then ten more every five minutes, up to a hundred and
;; fifty; the race's sampler and the machine's sampler record every fifteen seconds, and the
;; report finds the most bots a runner carries healthy and how to split its memory. Generous
;; heaps here, so the measure is what the JVMs use, not what they were given.
{:race/runners 20
 :race/bots 150            ; the ramp's top
 :race/prefix "Clj_c"
 :race/until "nether"
 :race/timeout-ms 4800000  ; a bot that joins at once races 80 minutes
 :race/deadline-ms 4800000 ; every bot stops 80 minutes after the first joined, however late it joined
 :race/stagger-ms 3000
 :race/ramp #:ramp{:start 10 :step 10 :every-ms 300000}
 :race/server-heap-mb 6144
 :race/bot-heap-mb 8192
 :race/max-players 200}
